Reuse the echo canceller's filter from before recording started again, moved by whole samples

Patch 0017 tries the refined filter from before recording started again at the next new
delay, moved by whole partitions (64 samples) only. In 12 of 40 changes in the call lab
it was not reused; the delay found after the restart seems to come back a few ms off,
less than a block, and then the old filter fits no whole partition.

Now the trial (Subtractor::StartFilterReuseTrial) tries the saved filter moved by
-kReuseMaxShiftSamples to +kReuseMaxShiftSamples samples (-512 to +512, the same reach
as 0017's -8 to +8 partitions) in steps of kReuseShiftStepSamples, 65 candidates
instead of 17. A move of N samples gives the filter whose sample n is sample n + N of
the saved one (for N = 64 k, 0017's "partition p takes partition p + k"). It is made in
two steps: by whole partitions, k = N / 64 rounded down (0017's shift), and then by the
samples left, r = N - 64 k, from 0 to 63 (SampleShiftedFilter: each partition's inverse
FFT gives its 64 taps, the first 64 samples scaled by 1/64, as AdaptiveFirFilter's
Constrain takes them; the whole response is moved by r, what goes past its start
dropped and the end filled with zeros, and cut back into partitions of 64 taps and 64
zeros by FFT; with r = 0 the filter is kept as it is). For a move back by a part of a
partition (N < 0, not a multiple of 64) the response's last r samples come out zero, as
the whole-partition step dropped them first.

The candidates are made once, at the trial's start; each trial block still filters
the render once and takes one inverse FFT per candidate, now for 65 of them. Nothing
else of 0017 changes: the best candidate is put in use when its residual is under
kReuseMaxResidual and its gain within [1/kReuseMaxGain, kReuseMaxGain]. The log says
"AEC3: filter from before recording started again reused, moved N samples, gain G,
residual R, B blocks after the restart"; when the best candidate fails either test, it
says "AEC3: filter from before recording started again not reused: best moved N samples,
gain G, residual R, B blocks after the restart" at the trial's end (a trial cut short by
a new delay, a flush or the window's end logs nothing). Delay changes while the reused
filter is in use still shift it by whole partitions, as in 0017.

Constants (Subtractor): kReuseMaxShiftSamples 512 (kReuseMaxShiftPartitions x 64),
kReuseShiftStepSamples 16; from 0017, unchanged: kReuseWindowBlocks 2500,
kReuseTrialBlocks 25, kReuseMaxResidual 0.5, kReuseMaxGain 1.41.

Measured: not yet.

